<title>USA: ServiceMaster declares Q2 payoyut, sees Q4 rise.</title>
<headline>ServiceMaster declares Q2 payoyut, sees Q4 rise.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNERS GROVE, Ill. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>ServiceMaster LP said Monday it set a cash distribution of $0.17 a share for the second quarter, and expects to raise the payout for the fourth quarter to $0.18 a share.</p>
<p>The third quarter dividend is expected to be $0.17 a share, equal to the second quarter level. The second quarter distribution is payable April 30 to shareholders of record on April 18.</p>
<p>ServiceMaster said the payouts are in line with its previously announced distribution policy for 1997, which provides for $0.69 a share annually.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
